---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DraftHeader from '../../components/draft/DraftHeader.astro';
import DraftContact from '../../components/draft/DraftContact.astro';
import DraftCaseNav from '../../components/draft/DraftCaseNav.astro';
import '../../styles/case-study.css';
import '../../styles/draft.css';

import travelHome from '../../assets/images/raa-travel-home.png';
import qtbStart from '../../assets/images/raa-qtb-start.png';
import raaWebsite from '../../assets/images/raa-website-home.png';
import myAccount from '../../assets/images/my-account.png';
import claimsFigma from '../../assets/images/raa-claims-figma.png';
import idmFigma from '../../assets/images/raa-idm-figma.png';
import paymentsFigma from '../../assets/images/raa-payments-figma.png';
import myaccountFigma from '../../assets/images/raa-myaccount-figma.png';
import appDsAlerts from '../../assets/images/raa-app-ds-alerts.png';
import dsButtons from '../../assets/images/raa-ds-buttons.png';
import mobileFlows from '../../assets/images/figma-mobile-app-screen-flows.png';
import freelance1a from '../../assets/images/freelance-1a.png';
import freelance2a from '../../assets/images/freelance-2a.png';
import freelance3a from '../../assets/images/freelance-3a.png';
import freelance4a from '../../assets/images/freelance-4a.png';
---
<Layout title="UI Design and Working with UI Teams | Andrew Smith" description="How a senior UX lead works with UI design leads and external vendors across RAA digital products, using low-fidelity prototypes built within the design system, tested, and iterated." showFooterCta={false}>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
  <div class="case-page">
    <DraftHeader />
    <main id="main-content">

      <section class="case-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow"><a class="breadcrumb-link" href="/portfolio/">Work</a><span class="breadcrumb-separator">/</span><span>UI design and working with UI teams</span></p>
        <h1 class="display-title">UI design and working with UI teams.</h1>
        <p class="hero-text">I am trained and experienced in UI. Over the years I have done the UI design and the front-end code for many projects, especially freelance work and new products.</p>
        <p class="hero-text">I write JavaScript and build websites. When a role needs it, I am confident doing UI end to end.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section no-border">
        <div class="section-content">
          <p class="section-kicker">Where I spend my time now</p>
          <p>In my recent roles, the more valuable use of that background has been running the UX process and working alongside dedicated UI design leads. Knowing UI principles, patterns and users' mental models means I prototype and test the right things, read an interface properly and make better recommendations.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="draft-ui-alongside">
        <p class="section-kicker">Working alongside UI teams</p>
        <p class="hero-text">Design agencies and UI designers delivered the first iteration of the RAA interface. Since then, as senior UX lead, I have worked with the UI design leads in my team and in other teams, and with external vendors, within Agile squads and the product trio. Starting in front-end development means working with engineers is a peer conversation, not a handover.</p>
        <p class="hero-subtext">Rapid, low-fidelity prototypes that work within the design system, tested with users and iterated for 800,000+ RAA members.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="meta-strip">
        <div><p class="meta-label">Scope</p><p class="meta-value">Travel, Insurance, Membership, Identity, Payments, Mobile</p></div>
        <div><p class="meta-label">Role</p><p class="meta-value">Senior UX Design Lead, UX Manager</p></div>
        <div><p class="meta-label">Tools</p><p class="meta-value">Figma, low-fidelity prototyping, usability testing, WCAG accessibility</p></div>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section">
        <div class="section-content">
          <p class="section-kicker">Products</p>
          <h2>Public-facing digital products used by members every day.</h2>
          <p>Led the UX on the RAA Travel platform after its initial rebuild, iterating with UI design leads across flights, stays, holidays, cruises, car hire, and experiences, on desktop and mobile. Led the UX for the RAA website redesign, working with external agencies and internal engineering.</p>
          <p>The quote and buy journey covers motor, home, and landlord insurance. Multiple rounds of usability testing, prototype iteration, and post-delivery benchmarking across each product area. Accessibility reviewed against WCAG 2.1 standards throughout, with ongoing audits through the Vision Australia partnership.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="scroll-section">
        <p class="scroll-hint-label">Scroll to see more <span>→</span></p>
        <div class="image-scroll-track-wrap">
          <div class="image-scroll-track">
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={travelHome} alt="RAA Travel homepage showing search widget, holiday deals, and navigation across product types" loading="eager" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>RAA Travel homepage — UX iterated with UI design leads across flights, stays, holidays, cruises, car hire, and experiences</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={raaWebsite} alt="RAA website homepage showing insurance, membership, motor, home, and travel navigation" loading="eager" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>RAA website homepage — UX led for the redesign, working with external agencies and internal engineering</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={qtbStart} alt="RAA Car Insurance quote start page showing step 1 of 4 with number plate lookup" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>Car insurance quote and buy — step one of four with My Account pre-fill prompt and progress stepper</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={myAccount} alt="RAA My Account member portal showing authenticated dashboard" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>My Account member portal — authenticated product managing insurance, membership, payments, and claims</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="content-section">
        <div class="section-content">
          <p class="section-kicker">Prototypes and Iteration</p>
          <h2>Low-fidelity prototypes that work within the design system.</h2>
          <p>I use my knowledge of UI fundamentals — typography, colour, layout, hierarchy, components, and accessibility — along with common interface patterns and users' mental models to build rapid, low-fidelity prototypes, layouts, and screens. They work within the design system and match what people expect, so ideas can be put in front of users quickly.</p>
          <p>Each round is tested, and the insights shape the next iteration with the UI design leads and the rest of the squad. The Figma files below show the breadth of product areas this covers — identity management and authentication, payments and renewals, claims submission, and the My Account portal.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="scroll-section">
        <p class="scroll-hint-label">Scroll to see more <span>→</span></p>
        <div class="image-scroll-track-wrap">
          <div class="image-scroll-track">
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={myaccountFigma} alt="Figma file showing My Account screens ready for dev across multiple features" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>My Account Figma file — ready-for-dev screens across multiple features including direct debit management</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={paymentsFigma} alt="Figma file showing online payments and renewals flow across multiple states" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>Payments and renewals Figma file — covering all product types, payment states, and validation scenarios</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={idmFigma} alt="Figma file showing identity management login flows including email, mobile, and password reset" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>Identity management — email login, mobile OTP, and password reset flows across all states and breakpoints</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={claimsFigma} alt="Figma file showing motor claims rebuild screens including review and lodge step" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>Motor claims rebuild — five-step claims flow with accessibility review and handoff specs included</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="content-section">
        <div class="section-content">
          <p class="section-kicker">Design System and Mobile</p>
          <h2>Working within a design system built for engineering adoption.</h2>
          <p>The RAA design system, built in-house by the team in Figma, covers web and mobile across all product areas. Alert components, button variants, form elements, and mobile-specific components all governed through a documented library with usage guidelines, anatomy, accessibility notes, and coded examples.</p>
          <p>Contributed UX to the RAA native app alongside senior mobile designers, covering screen flows, interaction patterns, and how mobile-specific design system components are used.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="scroll-section">
        <p class="scroll-hint-label">Scroll to see more <span>→</span></p>
        <div class="image-scroll-track-wrap">
          <div class="image-scroll-track">
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={appDsAlerts} alt="RAA app design system showing alert components across information, confirmation, warning, error, and helpful tip variants" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>RAA app design system — alert components showing all variants in light and dark mode with usage guidance</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={dsButtons} alt="Design system button documentation showing anatomy, spacing, typography, states, and accessibility guidelines" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>Button component documentation — anatomy, spacing, accessibility considerations, dos and don'ts, with coded examples</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={mobileFlows} alt="Figma prototype flow for RAA logbook mobile app showing connected screens" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>RAA app prototype flow — logbook feature showing all connected screens from entry through to drive recording</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="content-section">
        <div class="section-content">
          <p class="section-kicker">Freelance</p>
          <h2>Websites for clients across retail, health, and hospitality.</h2>
          <p>Running alongside full-time roles since 2004 — building websites and web applications for small to large clients. Each project starts from a template, and the build is iterated with the client. My focus is the UX work: scoping, content structure, navigation, and key flows, through to front-end development and delivery.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="scroll-section">
        <p class="scroll-hint-label">Scroll to see more <span>→</span></p>
        <div class="image-scroll-track-wrap">
          <div class="image-scroll-track">
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={freelance1a} alt="PALI Footwear ecommerce website — 100% New Zealand wool footwear brand" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>PALI Footwear — ecommerce site built from a template and iterated with an Australian wool footwear brand</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={freelance2a} alt="Chaircovers Over All hospitality ecommerce website" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>Chaircovers Over All — hospitality ecommerce site built and iterated with the client, plus product photography direction</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={freelance3a} alt="Bronwyn yoga and wellness website" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>Bronwyn yoga — website built and iterated with an independent yoga instructor</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="scroll-fig wide">
              <Image class="scroll-img-wide" src={freelance4a} alt="Bass Coast Podiatry clinic website" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[700,1000]} sizes="700px"/>
              <figcaption>Bass Coast Podiatry — website built from a template for a regional podiatry clinic</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <DraftCaseNav />
    </main>
    <DraftContact />
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
.scroll-fig.wide { width: 560px; }
.scroll-img-wide { width: 560px; height: 340px; object-fit: cover; object-position: top center; border-radius: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(23,23,23,.07); display: block; }
@media(max-width:860px) { .scroll-fig.wide { width: 320px; } .scroll-img-wide { width: 320px; height: 200px; } }
</style>
